         <div type="edition" xml:lang="tel-Latn">
            <p>
              <lb n="1"/>śrī śailamuni 
            </p>
         </div>
         <div type="apparatus">       
         </div>
         <div type="translation" resp="part:jeth">
 	  <p>
 	  Śrī Śailamuni
 	  </p>
         </div>
         <div type="commentary">
            <p>
              The name was found on <cit><quote>a beam in the verandah of the seventh cave temple at Bhairavakoṇḍa</quote><bibl><ptr target="bib:RamayyaPantulu1948_01"/><citedRange unit="page">19</citedRange></bibl></cit>. The nature of the name (≈ "holy man of the mountain (perh. Himalaya)" may rather point towards a high ranking religious person who visited the place than towards a craftsman who worked there; he might, however, have been a donor as well.
            </p>
         </div>
        <div type="bibliography">
          <p>
           The inscription was noted in A. R. No. 278 of 1922<!-- has to be adjusted to the @target --> and was first edited by J. Ramayya Pantulu with few metadata and without picture (<bibl rend="omitname"><ptr target="bib:RamayyaPantulu1948_01"/><citedRange unit="page">19</citedRange><citedRange unit="item">53</citedRange></bibl>). 
          </p>
           <listBibl type="secondary">
